Subject: [PATCH] 4656: every refused token leaves one log line (route and
 reason, never the token)

Tornike's computer asks for the phone login on every open. The app wipes
its token on any 401, and the server logged none, so the refusing call
could not be named. authenticateJwt now logs missing_header, invalid or
expired with the method and the route (no query), and expired_at for an
expired token. FOR_FRONTEND: the server's side, and three things on the
app's side (the 401 handler leaves the cookie; the apex to www redirect;
the start page's store).

